Name: frameImageData

Type: property

Syntax: get the frameImageData of <image>

Summary:
Returns the raw ARGB pixel data for the current <frame> of an
<animated GIF>.

Associations: image

Introduced: 1.1.0

OS: mac, windows, linux

Platforms: desktop, server

Example:
set the currentFrame of image "myGIF" to 3
put the frameImageData of image "myGIF" into tPixels

Value:
The <frameImageData> of an <image> is binary data containing the
composited ARGB pixel values for the current frame, in the same format
as the <imageData> property.
This property is read-only and cannot be set.

Description:
Use the <frameImageData> <property> to obtain raw pixel data for a
specific <frame> of an <animated GIF> without altering playback or
triggering a repaint. Unlike setting <currentFrame> and reading
<imageData>, accessing <frameImageData> does not call layer_redrawall()
and does not visually disturb the animation.

The returned data contains one 32-bit ARGB value per pixel, in row-major
order, for the full canvas dimensions of the GIF.

Set <currentFrame> to the desired frame index before reading this
property.

For non-animated images, <frameImageData> returns the same value as
<imageData>.

To obtain the frame as encoded PNG data suitable for passing to LCB
widgets or setting on another image object, use <frameText> instead.

References: property (glossary), animated GIF (glossary),
frame (glossary), image (keyword), currentFrame (property),
frameCount (property), frameText (property), frameDuration (property),
imageData (property)

Tags: multimedia
